body:
## Pull request overview

This PR enables thinking mode for Gemini 3 models when accessed via OpenRouter by detecting the `@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider` npm package and configuring the appropriate `thinkingLevel` parameter. The implementation distinguishes between Gemini 3 models (which use `thinkingLevel: "HIGH"`) and Gemini 2.5 models (which use basic `includeThoughts: true`).

**Key Changes:**
- Added OpenRouter Gemini 3 detection using npm package identification
- Configured `thinkingLevel: "HIGH"` for Gemini 3 models to enable extended thinking
- Updated `@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider` package from 1.2.8 to 1.5.2

### Reviewed changes

Copilot reviewed 2 out of 3 changed files in this pull request and generated 1 comment.

| File | Description |
| ---- | ----------- |
| packages/opencode/src/provider/transform.ts | Added logic to detect OpenRouter Gemini 3 models and configure thinkingConfig with thinkingLevel for Gemini 3 vs basic includeThoughts for Gemini 2.5 |
| packages/opencode/package.json | Updated @openrouter/ai-sdk-provider dependency to version 1.5.2 |
| bun.lock | Updated lock file entries for @openrouter/ai-sdk-provider and its dependencies |


<details>
<summary>Comments suppressed due to low confidence (2)</summary>

**packages/opencode/src/provider/transform.ts:248**
* The condition doesn't handle OpenRouter with Gemini 2.5 models. When using OpenRouter with a Gemini 2.5 model (e.g., `google/gemini-2.5-pro-experimental`), the outer condition evaluates to false because:
- `isDirectGoogle` is false (providerID would be "openrouter", not "google")
- `isOpencodeGemini3` is false (not an opencode provider and not gemini-3)
- `isGemini3ViaOpenRouter` is false (model.api.id doesn't include "gemini-3")

This means Gemini 2.5 models via OpenRouter won't get any `thinkingConfig` set.

Consider adding a check for OpenRouter Gemini 2.5 models:
```typescript
const isGeminiViaOpenRouter = 
  model.api.npm === "@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider" && 
  (model.api.id.includes("gemini-3") || model.api.id.includes("gemini-2"))
```
Then use `isGeminiViaOpenRouter` in the outer condition instead of `isGemini3ViaOpenRouter`.
```
      // Gemini 3 uses thinkingLevel, Gemini 2.5 uses thinkingBudget
      // For Gemini 3, we must use thinkingLevel: "HIGH" (not thinkingBudget)
      const isGemini3 = model.api.id.includes("gemini-3")
      result["thinkingConfig"] = {
        includeThoughts: true,
        ...(isGemini3 && { thinkingLevel: "HIGH" }),
      }
    }

    if (model.api.id.includes("gpt-5") && !model.api.id.includes("gpt-5-chat")) {
      if (model.providerID.includes("codex")) {
        result["store"] = false
      }

```
**packages/opencode/src/provider/transform.ts:248**
* The new Gemini thinking mode logic lacks test coverage. Consider adding tests to verify:
1. Direct Google Gemini 3 models get `thinkingLevel: "HIGH"`
2. Direct Google Gemini 2.5 models get basic `includeThoughts: true`
3. OpenRouter Gemini 3 models get `thinkingLevel: "HIGH"`
4. OpenCode Zen Gemini 3 models get `thinkingLevel: "HIGH"`

Example test structure in `packages/opencode/test/provider/transform.test.ts`:
```typescript
describe("ProviderTransform.options - Gemini thinkingConfig", () => {
  test("Direct Google Gemini 3 gets thinkingLevel HIGH", () => {
    const result = ProviderTransform.options(
      { providerID: "google", api: { id: "gemini-3-pro", npm: "@ai-sdk/google", url: "..." }, ... },
      "session-id"
    )
    expect(result.thinkingConfig).toEqual({ includeThoughts: true, thinkingLevel: "HIGH" })
  })
  // ... more tests
})
```
```
    // Enable thinking mode for Gemini models
    // - Direct Google: providerID === "google"
    // - OpenCode Zen with Gemini 3: providerID.startsWith("opencode") && model.api.id.includes("gemini-3")
    // - OpenRouter with Gemini 3: model.api.npm === "@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider" && model.api.id.includes("gemini-3")
    const isGemini3ViaOpenRouter = model.api.npm === "@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider" && model.api.id.includes("gemini-3")
    const isDirectGoogle = model.providerID === "google"
    const isOpencodeGemini3 = model.providerID.startsWith("opencode") && model.api.id.includes("gemini-3")

    if (isDirectGoogle || isOpencodeGemini3 || isGemini3ViaOpenRouter) {
      // Gemini 3 uses thinkingLevel, Gemini 2.5 uses thinkingBudget
      // For Gemini 3, we must use thinkingLevel: "HIGH" (not thinkingBudget)
      const isGemini3 = model.api.id.includes("gemini-3")
      result["thinkingConfig"] = {
        includeThoughts: true,
        ...(isGemini3 && { thinkingLevel: "HIGH" }),
      }
    }

    if (model.api.id.includes("gpt-5") && !model.api.id.includes("gpt-5-chat")) {
      if (model.providerID.includes("codex")) {
        result["store"] = false
      }

```
</details>



